# Frontend environment - PUBLIC values only. Copy to frontend/.env and fill in.
#
# Everything VITE_-prefixed is compiled into the JavaScript bundle that ships to
# the browser. Treat every value here as published.
#
# The publishable key is designed for exactly this: it identifies the project
# and carries no privileges of its own - what it may read or write is decided
# entirely by Row Level Security and table grants in the database.
#
# The service-role / secret key must NEVER appear in this file or any VITE_
# variable. It bypasses RLS. It belongs in the repository-root .env, which only
# the FastAPI backend reads.
#
# Both values: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API.
#
# The public key is read under either name - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (Supabase's
# older name for it, still used in most docs) or VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# (the newer one). They are the same credential; set whichever your dashboard
# shows and leave the other blank.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Absolute base for the FastAPI API, with no trailing slash.
#
# LOCAL: leave this empty. The app then uses relative URLs, which the Vite dev
# server proxies to http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see vite.config.js), so the browser
# stays on one origin and CORS never enters the picture.
#
# DEPLOYED: this MUST be set, because the dashboard is served as static files
# from a different origin than the API. Without it the built bundle would ask
# its own origin for /health, where nothing is listening. On Render it is set on
# the static site, not in this file:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://gridopt-api.onrender.com
# VITE_API_BASE=
